  "riskClass": "high",
  "title": "Onboard page stores applicationId in localStorage which persists after logout and across sessions",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: security. Severity: P1. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The onboard page stores the applicationId in localStorage after OTP verification. Unlike sessionStorage (which clears on tab close), localStorage persists indefinitely. If a user logs out and another person uses the same browser, the applicationId from the previous session is still accessible. This could allow the second user to resume or interfere with the first user's application. The register page correctly uses sessionStorage for the same purpose.",
